WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.906
In this video you will learn to find, read and
fix your measurements.

00:00:05.026 --> 00:00:10.402
You will search and filter your list, correct
a mistake, export a station's history,

00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:14.026
and see what happens to a visit saved with no
signal.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:19.362
To see everything you have recorded, choose My
measurements in the menu.

00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:24.863
This page lists every measurement from your
stations, newest first.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:27.767
The line under the title says how many.

00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:30.959
This grey note is a reminder.

00:00:31.079 --> 00:00:34.871
The numbers are contributed by users and are
not verified.

00:00:34.991 --> 00:00:38.063
Always test drinking water in a laboratory.

00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:44.979
Upload data file adds many measurements at once from
a spreadsheet, for the stations you may record at.

00:00:45.099 --> 00:00:47.979
Most people add one visit at a time.

00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:54.927
Each line is one measurement: the station and its
code, the kind of station, what was measured,

00:00:55.047 --> 00:00:57.207
and the value with its unit.

00:00:58.017 --> 00:01:01.089
Then the date and time, and who added it.

00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:04.941
Slide the table sideways to find Notes.

00:01:05.061 --> 00:01:08.541
Here the person wrote what they saw and how
they measured.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.278
Status shows where a measurement stands.

00:01:12.398 --> 00:01:15.086
Recorded means it has been saved.

00:01:15.917 --> 00:01:18.989
Needs review means someone should look again.

00:01:19.109 --> 00:01:22.181
Checked means it has been looked at and
accepted.

00:01:22.301 --> 00:01:24.725
You only read these labels.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:30.494
If the visit included a photo, a small picture
appears beside the value.

00:01:31.317 --> 00:01:34.845
If it included a video, press the round play
button.

00:01:34.965 --> 00:01:37.917
It opens full screen, with sound.

00:01:38.037 --> 00:01:40.485
Close it with Close or Escape.

00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:44.941
To find a station, type part of its name or
code.

00:01:45.061 --> 00:01:49.165
The list shortens as you type, and matches are
highlighted.

00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:53.871
To narrow the list in more ways, press Show
filters.

00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:58.835
At the top, pick one station to see only its
measurements.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.746
Station type keeps one kind of station.

00:02:02.866 --> 00:02:06.394
Measurement type then offers only that kind's
measures.

00:02:07.217 --> 00:02:10.937
From date and To date keep measurements
between two days.

00:02:11.057 --> 00:02:13.313
The To date day is included.

00:02:14.117 --> 00:02:17.405
Nothing changes until you press Apply filters.

00:02:17.525 --> 00:02:21.941
Then only those rainfall measurements are
left, and the count changes.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:26.974
Clear filters puts everything back, including
the search box.

00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:30.447
Click a column title to sort the list.

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.727
Click again to flip the order.

00:02:32.847 --> 00:02:35.151
The arrow shows the direction.

00:02:35.983 --> 00:02:40.279
Click Measurement date and time twice to bring
the newest back to the top.

00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:44.371
The list shows twenty-five measurements at a
time.

00:02:44.491 --> 00:02:46.867
Press Next for the following page.

00:02:47.683 --> 00:02:53.827
At the end of each line, the map icon shows the
station on the map, and Edit fixes a mistake.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.522
Press Edit.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:03:01.442
The details are already filled in, and the
title shows the measurement number.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.482
The station cannot change.

00:03:04.602 --> 00:03:07.578
A measurement always stays with its station.

00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:12.199
You can change the date and time, but not to
the future.

00:03:13.017 --> 00:03:15.633
Measurement type is the kind of measure.

00:03:15.753 --> 00:03:18.057
Measurement value is the number.

00:03:18.177 --> 00:03:20.049
Type the correct one.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:25.986
Notes are for anything the next person should
know, such as why you changed the number.

00:03:26.817 --> 00:03:30.369
Photo and Video show what was saved with this
visit.

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:33.153
You can add a new one or remove it.

00:03:33.983 --> 00:03:40.607
People allowed to delete, such as organisation
administrators, also see a red Delete button here,

00:03:40.727 --> 00:03:42.863
and it asks to confirm.

00:03:42.983 --> 00:03:45.359
A Data Contributor does not.

00:03:46.183 --> 00:03:48.247
Press Save changes.

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:52.351
You land on the station's measurements, with
the corrected number.

00:03:53.183 --> 00:03:55.439
This is the station's history.

00:03:55.559 --> 00:03:59.255
The small number on Show filters says one
filter is on.

00:04:00.083 --> 00:04:06.155
Export, Excel, saves this station's measurements as
a spreadsheet, following your dates.

00:04:06.275 --> 00:04:10.091
It appears on a station's history, not the
main list.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:16.701
A measurement saved with no signal waits on your
phone, in this box called Waiting to upload.

00:04:17.517 --> 00:04:21.741
With signal they send by themselves, or press
Retry now.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:27.021
A visit the server refuses stays, in red,
under Refused measurements.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:33.154
Delete asks once more, because a visit that
never uploaded cannot be recovered.

00:04:33.983 --> 00:04:36.383
Confirm, and it is gone.

00:04:36.503 --> 00:04:39.719
The visits that sent are now at the top of
your list.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:43.238
That is how you look after your measurements.

00:04:43.358 --> 00:04:50.534
Search, filter and sort to find them, press Edit to fix a
mistake, and export a history when you need it.

00:04:50.654 --> 00:04:53.318
Thanks for helping look after our water.
